# Workers static assets are collected from assets.directory ("." = repo root).
# Unlike Pages, Workers does NOT auto-exclude node_modules/.git, and it does
# NOT consult .cfignore (that is a Pages-only mechanism). List everything that
# must not be uploaded/served as a public asset here.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore-style. A bare name (e.g. `scripts`) matches that name
# at ANY depth — which would wrongly exclude assets/scripts/. So:
#   - use `**/<name>` for "anywhere" matches (build cruft)
#   - use a leading `/` to anchor a path to the repo root (top-level dirs)
#
# Keep served: index.html, sw.js, _headers, assets/**, and the data files the
# app fetches at runtime (data/*.jsonl, data/sages.json, data/version.json,
# data/jastrow-abbr.json, data/jastrow-hebrew-abbr.json).

# Build/runtime cruft anywhere in the tree (the 53 MiB biome binary lives
# under node_modules and exceeds the 25 MiB per-file asset limit).
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.DS_Store

# Local-only tooling, source, and docs — anchored to repo root so the
# app's own assets/ subtree (assets/scripts, assets/styles) is NOT excluded.
/data/admin
/data/raw
/docs
/scripts
/.github
/.claude
/.vscode
/.remember
/.wrangler
/biome.json
/package.json
/bun.lock
/tsconfig.json
/wrangler.jsonc
/renovate.json
/.commitlintrc.ts
/.editorconfig
/.mise.toml
/.gitignore
/.gitattributes
/.cfignore
/.assetsignore
/README.md
/CONTRIBUTING.md
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
/SECURITY.md
/DCO
/LICENSE

# TypeScript sources anywhere (admin tooling); the deployed site is plain JS.
**/*.ts
